    "prompt": "KMeans clustering currently produces slightly different results when run with a single thread (n_jobs=1) compared to parallel execution. In this feature the goal is to fix the single\u2010thread execution path so that the random seed generation is performed only once and then applied consistently to each run. This is achieved by moving the generation of the random seeds outside of the iteration loop and then using each seed for every initialization when running in single-thread mode. After the fix, users should observe that the inertia values and clustering labels remain fully reproducible when using n_jobs=1, matching the expected behavior.",
