  "feature2": {
    "prompt": "In KMeans clustering the results produced by parallel execution (n_jobs > 1) should be identical to those obtained from single-threaded runs. However, redundant generation of random seeds in the parallel execution branch may lead to discrepancies in the clustering outcomes. This feature addresses the removal of the redundant seed generation in the parallel branch so that the same random state logic is applied consistently. After the fix, whether KMeans is run in parallel or single-threaded mode, the inertia values and labels should be identical, ensuring reproducibility and optimized performance.",
    "hint_texts": "Work in the same k_means function in sklearn/cluster/k_means_.py but focus on the else branch where n_jobs > 1 is handled. Remove the secondary call that generates seeds redundant to the one already computed. Ensure that the parallel execution path does not independently call random_state.randint, and validate that the modified behavior matches the single-threaded results.",
    "entrypoint": "File: sklearn/cluster/k_means_.py; Function: k_means; Location: in the else branch after the effective_n_jobs(n_jobs) check (around line 378 and afterward). The job is to remove the additional seed generation so that only the precomputed seeds are used in the overall execution.",
